<title>INDIA: Indian soybean steady, oil up, meal down.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean steady, oil up, meal down.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean prices were almost steady in the markets of central India on Wednesday as demand and supply were both equal, dealers said. Business volume was good and the undertone was steady.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices were up by 100 rupees per tonne on good demand in local markets. Business volume was good and the undertone was steady.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction prices were down on increased selling. Soymeal yellow was $317 per tonne FAS (Free alongside ship) for west coast at Indian ports. Rapeseed extraction was $117 per tonne FAS for west coast at Indian ports and was 4,100 rupees per tonne in FOR (Free on Rail) condition. Business volume was dull and the undertone was easy.</p>
